  "audit_contract": [
    "Root supplies final unique trigger/run/result commit. Publish an exact metadata and raw-artifact input receipt before reading any new diagnostic binary.",
    "Verify pinned producer/source binding/helper/runtime/scope/attempt identities and every compressed/raw byte size/SHA256. Decode new gzip through base64 only. Preserve incomplete/failed outcomes and never execute retrieval.",
    "Parse JSON integer tokens exactly with BigInt; distinguish bool/float/exponent tokens from integer counters/timestamps. Re-emit exact integer tokens with a BigInt-aware JSON serializer.",
    "Require eight ordered cells, original dataset and whole query schedule/universe hashes,4732 complete rows and direct comparison of every complete non-timing payload digest with the eight frozenC2 references.",
    "Independently reconstruct each raw span's parent tree and entry preorder. Validate exact sequence/site IDs, completed native return/exception status, nonnegative integer clocks, parent containment, nonoverlapping sibling/root intervals including shared-tick legal cases, child-inclusive sums, inclusive/exclusive arithmetic and event/wall/residual totals.",
    "Independently recompute source category from the frozen file SHA/function/line/upper-caller rules; preserve explicit other/unclassified/disabled categories and all exceptions. Unknown primary or disabled usage cannot yield accepted completion.",
    "Reaggregate all raw spans by cell/category and by callsite/method, compare every declared callsite_summary entry/count/duration, and report exact per-cell event counts, native/fallback fetch-site counts, recall-wall/exclusive/unattributed/bookkeeping totals. No top-N reduction or inferred SQL text.",
    "Inclusive parent/child totals can overlap and are not additive wall time. Exclusive builtin spans still contain Python callbacks/scheduling/instrumentation. Unattributed time is never labeled Python-only; no overhead subtraction, speed claim, unprofiled estimate or NO improvement percentage.",
    "Audit code/artificial negative fixtures and receipts live only on the independent validation branch. Existing source/controller/correctness, original scopes/helpers and author/root branches remain untouched."
  ],
